// wolf-lang#431, the same defect without the deadlock.
//
// The witness beside this one hangs, which costs 60 s to observe and
// says only "something never finished". This one answers in
// milliseconds and says WHAT: the task's capture record is read after
// the frame that holds it is gone.
//
// `fan_out` does not open the scope — it receives the handle — so the
// capture record `s174` found lands in `fan_out`'s own frame slot
// (`pack_task_env`'s `arena: None` arm, `crates/wolf_wir/src/lower.rs`),
// and `fan_out` returns before the queued task reads it. On the
// Cranelift tier the task therefore prints an address instead of `7`,
// a different one every run. On the LLVM tier it prints `7` — which is
// luck about frame reuse, not soundness, and is why this file asserts
// the VALUE on both tiers rather than asserting the two tiers agree.

fn fan_out(s: Scope, n: int) {
    s.spawn(fn() { print("task-{n}") })
}

fn main() -> !int {
    scope work {
        fan_out(work, 7)
    }
    0
}
